(## Push Notifications Ч How It Works) Tj
0 -13 Td
() Tj
0 -13 Td
(1. On login \(in a native EAS build\), the app calls `registerPushToken\(\)` which:) Tj
0 -13 Td
(   - Requests notification permissions from the OS) Tj
0 -13 Td
(   - Gets an Expo Push Token from the Expo service) Tj
0 -13 Td
(   - Registers it with the ACES API at `PUT /api/technicians/:id/fcm-token`) Tj
0 -13 Td
(2. When an admin assigns a mission in the web portal, the API sends a push notification via `https://exp.host/--) Tj
0 -13 Td
(  /api/v2/push/send`) Tj
0 -13 Td
(3. The technician receives the notification even if the app is in the background) Tj
0 -13 Td
() Tj
0 -13 Td
(> The push notification delivery code \(`lib/push.ts`\) uses a dynamic import so it gracefully skips registration ) Tj
0 -13 Td
(  in Expo Go and web previews, avoiding any runtime errors.) Tj
0 -13 Td
() Tj
0 -13 Td
(---) Tj
0 -13 Td
() Tj
0 -13 Td
